From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:05:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 263/342] Shutdown: turn the display off before powering off;
 usb_hid: no repeats of a stuck button

registrar: a machine that can't cut its own power (the ODROID-C2) went on
showing the last picture after powering off, a blank desktop: DPMS off just
before _kern_shutdown(), and on again if that fails, for the shutdown window.

usb_hid: buttons with a bit each (headsets, USB audio adapters, 6387c5d7f7)
repeated like keys. An adapter that reads "play" as held sent the key 25 times
a second for ever, and each one reset the screen saver's idle time. Of these
only volume up and down repeat now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp     | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 src/servers/registrar/ShutdownProcess.cpp      | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp
index 646082a7cb..fb589b5ef2 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp
@@ -835,9 +835,21 @@ KeyboardProtocolHandler::_ReadReport(bigtime_t timeout, uint32 *cookie)
 			_WriteKey(key, keyDown);
 
 			if (keyDown) {
-				// repeat handling
-				fCurrentRepeatKey = key;
-				fCurrentRepeatDelay = fRepeatDelay;
+				// repeat handling; of the buttons with a bit each (headsets,
+				// USB audio adapters) only volume up and down repeat: such a
+				// button can read as held for good (an adapter's "play"),
+				// and its repeats would count as input for ever, so the
+				// screen saver would never start
+				bool onOffControl = !fKeys[i]->Array()
+					&& fKeys[i]->UsagePage() != B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_KEYBOARD;
+				if (!onOffControl
+					|| key == ((B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_CONSUMER << 16)
+						| B_HID_UID_CON_VOLUME_INCREMENT)
+					|| key == ((B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_CONSUMER << 16)
+						| B_HID_UID_CON_VOLUME_DECREMENT)) {
+					fCurrentRepeatKey = key;
+					fCurrentRepeatDelay = fRepeatDelay;
+				}
 			} else {
 				// cancel the repeats if they are for this key
 				if (fCurrentRepeatKey == key) {
diff --git a/src/servers/registrar/ShutdownProcess.cpp b/src/servers/registrar/ShutdownProcess.cpp
index fadc960fa9..e7747de907 100644
--- a/src/servers/registrar/ShutdownProcess.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/registrar/ShutdownProcess.cpp
@@ -1197,7 +1197,20 @@ status_t
 ShutdownProcess::_ShutDown()
 {
 	PRINT("Invoking _kern_shutdown(%d)\n", fReboot);
-	RETURN_ERROR(_kern_shutdown(fReboot));
+
+	// A machine that can't cut its own power (the ODROID-C2) goes on showing
+	// the last picture after powering off: turn the display off first.
+	if (fReboot || !fHasGUI)
+		RETURN_ERROR(_kern_shutdown(fReboot));
+
+	BScreen screen;
+	bool displayOff = screen.SetDPMS(B_DPMS_OFF) == B_OK;
+	status_t status = _kern_shutdown(fReboot);
+
+	// It failed: the shutdown window has something to say now.
+	if (displayOff)
+		screen.SetDPMS(B_DPMS_ON);
+	RETURN_ERROR(status);
 }
 
 
